{"title":"Career roadmap · Real Estate Executive","role":"Real Estate Executive","summary":"Career alignment: A Real Estate Executive supports the business and operational side of property development, sales, leasing, property management, real estate investment, brokerage and construction-linked projects.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role combines real estate knowledge + sales + finance + market research + property documentation + customer management + digital tools + analytics. A BBA graduate does not need to become a civil engineer to build a strong real-estate career, but should understand the technical and construction concepts necessary to work effectively with engineers, architects, contractors and developers."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Role","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Real Estate Executive"},{"text":"Sales, leasing, documentation or operations"}],[{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Real Estate Analyst / Property Executive"},{"text":"Market, sales, leasing and property analysis"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Senior Real Estate Executive / Assistant Manager"},{"text":"Portfolio, sales or property operations"}],[{"text":"4–7 years"},{"text":"Real Estate Manager / Project Business Manager"},{"text":"Property/project management"}],[{"text":"6–10 years"},{"text":"Senior Real Estate Manager / Development Manager"},{"text":"Project and commercial leadership"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Head of Real Estate / Business Head"},{"text":"Portfolio and strategic management"}],[{"text":"Entrepreneurial"},{"text":"Real Estate Entrepreneur / Developer"},{"text":"Property development and investment"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During BBA","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Business & Real Estate Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Business fundamentals"}